    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "History",
            "paragraphs": [
                "The Chinese Workers Mutual Aid Club, located at 12 Bateman Street, Soho, is one of the longest-established Chinese community institutions in London's Chinatown. The organisation was formally incorporated in 1962 as The Chinese Mutual Aid Workers Club Limited, although its roots go back to 1907.",
                "The club was established to provide mutual support, social welfare, and community facilities for Chinese workers and residents at a time when many faced language barriers, discrimination, and limited access to mainstream services. Situated in the heart of Chinatown, it became an important social hub where members could meet, organise community activities, and maintain cultural connections."
            ]
        }
    ],
